{"_":"Font Awesome's categories in the emoji picker (1.71.0, assets/js/emoji-picker.js): the icon each category's chip shows in place of its name — or a short run of icons where that reads better (A B C, 1 2 3, B I U, ? ! &, an apple and a carrot) — the name being the chip's tooltip and what a screen reader says. The ids are Font Awesome's own (the same 68 in the owner's 6.7.2 and 7.3.1 indexes) and the catalogue's two made-up pages, brands and other. This project's choice of Font Awesome icon NAMES, every one of them in both of the owner's Pro packages; nothing of Font Awesome's files. A chip is drawn in the picker's own default for each icon: the site's emoji style where the icon has it, else the classic family at that weight. A category with no entry here, or whose icon the package in use lacks, shows `fallback`.",
